<title>NEW ZEALAND: NZ ADRs mostly stronger in NY as Dow leaps 47 pts.</title>
<headline>NZ ADRs mostly stronger in NY as Dow leaps 47 pts.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>New Zealand ADRs were mostly stronger in afternoon New York trade, where the Dow Industrials leaped 47.71 points after incumbent U.S. president Bill Clinton was returned to power.</p>
<p>Price movements of NZ stocks listed in the U.S., Britain and Australia.</p>
<p>Company		   Exchange    Last	  Net change</p>
<p>Tranz Rail   N.Y.    US$17	     +0 1/8  *</p>
<p>FCL Bldg	 N.Y.    US$27 1/2	 +0 3/8  *</p>
<p>FCL Engy	 N.Y.    US$28 1/2	 -0 1/4  *</p>
<p>FCL Paper	 N.Y.    US$18 3/4	 +0 1/8  *</p>
<p>FCL Forest     N.Y.    US$16 1/4	 +0 1/8  *</p>
<p>Telecom	  N.Y.    US$85 3/4	 +2 1/8  *</p>
<p>Thistle	  London  160		   -1</p>
<p>Guinness Peat  London  33		  +0 1/2</p>
<p>Brierley	 London  53		  +24.99</p>
<p>NZ IT	    London  238 1/2	     +1</p>
<p>Foreign &amp; Col London  150 1/2	   +0 1/2</p>
<p>Templeton	London  131 1/2	   +1 1/4</p>
<p>Lion	    Sydney  A$3.35		nil</p>
<p>Goodman	 Sydney  A$1.50		nil</p>
<p>Macraes	 Sydney  A$3.18		nil</p>
<p>Notes - In New York, Telecom's American Depository Receipts are traded in bundles of 16 shares, while both the Fletcher Challenge shares are in bundles of 10 each. Tranz Rail ADSs are groups of three ordinary shares.</p>
<p>- London prices are mid-rates.</p>
<p>- Asterisk * means stock is still trading</p>
<p>-- Wellington Newsroom 64 4 4734 746</p>
